  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multiprofile + avgpool + PCA (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. Avgpool outperforms transformer (0.591 vs 0.519). The key unresolved question is whether combining the strong RNA signal with image features via multimodal fusion can surpass the RNA-only baseline. Config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA n2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) pairs the proven-best RNA pipeline (multiprofile + avgpool + PCA) with the only image encoder we have evidence for (ResNet50) and uses the simplest fusion (concat). This is the most informative next step: if it beats 0.591, the entire multimodal design space (ViT-L, weighted fusion, learned RNA encoders) becomes worth exploring; if it does not, we can confidently redirect remaining budget toward improving the RNA encoder (scvi/scgpt) rather than investing in image-side improvements. It is the minimal, clean test of the fusion hypothesis using all currently validated components."
}

